    "body": "On top of #36765, this extends FuzzedSock to report more events a real OS could report (see #36737 for some coverage of those), and improves the connman fuzz target to assert more socket handling invariants.\n\nThe first commit is also a fix to uniquely identify sockets, as currently each socket can only use one of two descriptor values, which means the fuzz target would act on one peer with the event of another.\n\nSee commit messages for details.",
