      "parents": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/94181c18e25436d5e4a2de2ff71714413b4552a2",
          "sha": "94181c18e25436d5e4a2de2ff71714413b4552a2",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/94181c18e25436d5e4a2de2ff71714413b4552a2"
        }
      ],
      "message": "fuzz: push a message to an actually connected node in connman target\n\nPushing a message to random_node, which is never part of connman's\nm_nodes, meant that whatever data left in vSendMsg was never picked up,\nand that actual peers in m_nodes mostly never had anything to send (the\nqueue of all nodes added with AddTestNode() was always empty, and the\nv2 peers only ever had their handshake bytes to send).\n\nFix this by pushing messages to a peer chosen amongst connman's m_nodes\ninstead, to increase meaningful coverage of connman's operations.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Antoine Poinsot",
        "email": "mail@antoinep.com",
        "date": "2026-11-04T19:50:57Z"
