          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/ad51e87ecfd8f4b27e703b5c6116e6d75dcb9787"
        }
      ],
      "message": "fuzz: give each FuzzedSock its own socket\n\nPrior to this commit, every FuzzedSock had one of two socket values and\nCConnman::SocketHandler() merged the entries of different peers in a\nsingle wait, which led the connman fuzz target to act on one peer with\nthe events of another.\n\nThis fixes it by using a different descriptor value for each socket,\nlike the OS does for real sockets. This is achieved by numbering the\nsockets down from a global counter, restarted before each fuzz input to\nkeep each run deterministic.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Antoine Poinsot",
        "email": "mail@antoinep.com",
        "date": "2026-11-05T19:25:05Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "Antoine Poinsot",
        "email": "mail@antoinep.com",
        "date": "2026-11-03T18:30:24Z"
      },
      "sha": "111a2f779437c8a37fc4cd4eedd027a741163a92"
    },
    {
